"asr": "Scientists from Los Alamos in San Diego came to Taos to hunt a sound most people there cannot hear. Hearers said it throbbed like an idling diesel engine. New Mexico's congressman had asked for the hunt. An Air Force lab joined in. The team set out microphones, seismic sensors and magnetometers. They caught lightning, the power grid and a tunneling gopher. No hum. Hearers matched it to tones from about 33 to 80 hertz. In 1993 their ear expert ruled out tinnitus. He wondered if their ears were making the sound. But in 2026 a study of 28 hearers blamed tinnitus. For many, not all. It found no sounds coming from their ears either. And it couldn't rule out a real hum out there. Nobody explained it."
